<title>TURKEY: Turk Migros to raise capital, pay dividend.</title>
<headline>Turk Migros to raise capital, pay dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's leading supermarket chain Migros T.A.S. said it planned to raise its capital to 945 billion lira from 540 and pay a 500 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 1996 profits.</p>
<p>In a statement sent to the Istanbul Stock Exchange, Migros said it planned to issue 405 billion lira of bonuses, or 0.75 for one existing share. The capital increase is subject to approval by the regulatory Capital Markets Board.</p>
<p>The dividend proposal must also be approved at the company's annual meeting of shareholders and directors due on March 31.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
